<title>CANADA: CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</title>
<headline>CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vacant space in Canadian Prairie primary grain elevators fell to 27 percent in the week ended July 13, the Canadian Wheat Boad said.</p>
<p>The 27 percent elevator vacancy rate was down from 30 percent on July 6, the Board said.</p>
<p>Manitoba had the most space at 34 percent, followed by Alberta at 27 percent and Saskatchewan at 20 percent.</p>
<p>Vancouver unloaded 3,017 railcars versus the 3,300 target. Prince Rupert unloaded 1,243 railcars versus the 900 target. Thunder Bay unloaded 3,421 railcars versus the 3,550 target.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
